ICD issue Change 6.0 (R4.0) Acknowledgement flags can be changed at load time, disabling report-based stages 6.1 <code>CVS_TYPE</code>/<code>CVS_SOURCE</code> clarified: report-based progress stages only for step 0 (S2K-40-DCR-0821) 6.7 (R5.2) <code>CVS_UNCERTAINTY</code> added to override the TC SPACON window (S2K-SCR-3774); <code>CVS_ID</code> restricted to a signed short (S2K-DCR-3909) 6.9 <code>CVE_CVSID</code> and <code>CVP_CVSID</code> lengths aligned with <code>CVS_ID</code> as Number(5); <code>CVS_UNCERTAINTY</code> description updated (S2K-NCR-5531) <p><sup>19</sup><sup>20</sup></p> <p>The Solar Orbiter SWA instrument database still uses six-field <code>cvs</code> records (without <code>CVS_UNCERTAINTY</code>) and defines only the two stages 58901 and 58907, for all 198 of its commands.<sup>45</sup> Other projects attached meaning to stage numbers; the Herschel/Planck System database (HPSDB), for example, coded specific stages with four digits and generic ones as <code>1xxxx</code>.<sup>40</sup> More on mission conventions in Mission tailoring of the MIB.</p> SQL used <p>Queries ran with <code>sqlite3 -readonly</code> on this wiki's SQLite copy of the Solar Orbiter MIB (<code>solo-2025-09-16.sqlite</code>). The three verification tables are not in the automatic schema, so their columns are <code>COL1..COLn</code> in file order. From the ICD field order: <code>cvs</code> COL1 <code>CVS_ID</code>, COL2 <code>CVS_TYPE</code>, COL3 <code>CVS_SOURCE</code>, COL4 <code>CVS_START</code>, COL5 <code>CVS_INTERVAL</code>, COL6 <code>CVS_SPID</code>, COL7 <code>CVS_UNCERTAINTY</code>; <code>cve</code> COL1 <code>CVE_CVSID</code>, COL2 <code>CVE_PARNAM</code>, COL3 <code>CVE_INTER</code>, COL4 <code>CVE_VAL</code>, COL5 <code>CVE_TOL</code>, COL6 <code>CVE_CHECK</code>; <code>cvp</code> COL1 <code>CVP_TASK</code>, COL2 <code>CVP_TYPE</code>, COL3 <code>CVP_CVSID</code>.</p> <pre><code>SELECT COL2 AS type, COL3 AS source, count(*) FROM cvs GROUP BY 1, 2;
SELECT COL4, COL5, count(*) FROM cvs GROUP BY 1, 2 ORDER BY 3 DESC;
SELECT * FROM cvs WHERE COL6 &lt;&gt; '' ORDER BY cast(COL1 AS int);
-- profile shape per command, against the default Ack flags
SELECT c.CCF_ACK, ifnull(prof, '(none)'), count(*)
  FROM ccf c LEFT JOIN (SELECT p.COL1 AS cmd, group_concat(s.COL2 || s.COL3, '+') AS prof
                          FROM cvp p JOIN cvs s ON s.COL1 = p.COL3 GROUP BY p.COL1) x
    ON x.cmd = c.CCF_CNAME
 GROUP BY 1, 2;
-- report-based stages, their users and APIDs
SELECT s.COL1, s.COL2, s.COL5, s.COL6, count(p.COL1), group_concat(DISTINCT c.CCF_APID)
  FROM cvs s LEFT JOIN cvp p ON p.COL3 = s.COL1 LEFT JOIN ccf c ON c.CCF_CNAME = p.COL1
 WHERE s.COL3 = 'R' GROUP BY s.COL1 ORDER BY cast(s.COL1 AS int);
-- expressions
SELECT e.*, f.PCF_DESCR, f.PCF_NATUR, f.PCF_USCON FROM cve e LEFT JOIN pcf f ON f.PCF_NAME = e.COL2;
SELECT SOURCE FROM synthetic WHERE NAME = 'NPWSX001';
-- Service 1 packets and their identification
SELECT * FROM pic WHERE PIC_TYPE = '1';
SELECT PID_STYPE, count(*), count(DISTINCT PID_APID) FROM pid WHERE PID_TYPE = '1' GROUP BY 1;
-- CEV disabled in sequences
SELECT CSS_SQNAME, CSS_ENTRY, CSS_ELEMID FROM css WHERE CSS_CEV = 'Y';
</code></pre>

Table April 2020 (<code>10720PFM</code>) September 2025 (<code>25925PFM</code>) <code>ccf</code> 5,238 5,454 <code>cpc</code> 6,947 7,155 <code>cdf</code> 44,944 47,609 <code>ptv</code> 0 5 <code>prf</code> / <code>prv</code> 531 / 631 565 / 1,072 <code>paf</code> / <code>pas</code> 605 / 9,741 624 / 11,834 <code>cca</code> / <code>ccs</code> 100 / 1,233 99 / 1,226 <code>tcp</code> / <code>pcpc</code> / <code>pcdf</code> / <code>dst</code> 4 / 6 / 20 / 1 4 / 7 / 20 / 1 <p><sup>37</sup><sup>38</sup></p> <p>The header layer changed in one place: in 2020 the <code>NOM_TC</code> Source ID was a fixed area with value 0, while in 2025 it is an element of type <code>O</code> linked to the new <code>pcpc</code> parameter <code>DFH_SRC</code> (see the note in The Solar Orbiter headers); the description of <code>NOM_TC</code> also changed from "Normal Header" to "NOM_DH_TC_Packet_Header". The growth is in commands, parameters and especially aliases and range values. The Solar Orbiter MIB page puts these numbers in the context of the whole database, and How Solar Orbiter uses PUS covers the services behind the commands.</p> SQL used <p>All queries ran with <code>sqlite3 -readonly</code> on this wiki's SQLite copy of the Solar Orbiter MIB (<code>solo-2025-09-16.sqlite</code>; <code>solo-2020-04-16.sqlite</code> and <code>swa-idb.sqlite</code> for the comparisons). Every column is stored as text, so numeric comparisons need <code>cast(... as int)</code>.</p> <pre><code>-- headers
SELECT * FROM tcp;
SELECT * FROM pcpc;
SELECT * FROM pcdf ORDER BY PCDF_TCNAME, cast(PCDF_BIT AS int);
SELECT CCF_PKTID, count(*) FROM ccf GROUP BY 1;
-- ccf profile
SELECT CCF_CTYPE, count(*) FROM ccf GROUP BY 1;
SELECT CCF_HIPRI, CCF_MAPID, count(*) FROM ccf GROUP BY 1, 2;
SELECT CCF_ACK, count(*) FROM ccf GROUP BY 1;
SELECT CCF_ILSCOPE, CCF_ILSTAGE, count(*) FROM ccf GROUP BY 1, 2;
SELECT sum(CCF_SUBSYS = CCF_SUBSCHEDID), sum(CCF_SUBSYS &lt;&gt; CCF_SUBSCHEDID) FROM ccf;
SELECT CCF_APID, count(*) FROM ccf GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC;
-- cdf / cpc profile
SELECT CDF_ELTYPE, CDF_INTER, count(*) FROM cdf GROUP BY 1, 2;
SELECT count(*), count(DISTINCT CDF_CNAME) FROM cdf WHERE cast(CDF_GRPSIZE AS int) &gt; 0;
SELECT count(*) FROM cdf WHERE CDF_TMID &lt;&gt; '';
SELECT CPC_PTC, CPC_PFC, count(*) FROM cpc GROUP BY 1, 2 ORDER BY 3 DESC;
SELECT CPC_CATEG, count(*) FROM cpc GROUP BY 1;
-- examples
SELECT d.*, c.* FROM cdf d LEFT JOIN cpc c ON c.CPC_NAME = d.CDF_PNAME
 WHERE CDF_CNAME = 'ZPW04604' ORDER BY cast(CDF_BIT AS int);
SELECT * FROM pas WHERE PAS_NUMBR IN ('CCDT0030TX', 'CCDT0031TX');
SELECT * FROM cca JOIN ccs ON CCS_NUMBR = CCA_NUMBR WHERE CCA_NUMBR = 'CAHP0000TC';
SELECT * FROM prf JOIN prv ON PRV_NUMBR = PRF_NUMBR WHERE PRF_NUMBR IN ('VCD00176', 'VCD00269');
SELECT p.*, f.PCF_DESCR, f.PCF_NATUR FROM ptv p LEFT JOIN pcf f ON f.PCF_NAME = p.PTV_PARNAM;
